```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason: Both queries return the same four correct record‑holders, but 2result.sql reaches those results with a simpler, clearer structure (one single‑row CTE that gathers the four maximum values, then four straightforward SELECT … UNION ALL blocks).  It avoids the extra “statistic” bookkeeping and extra joins found in 1result.sql, while still filtering out blank strings and casting text columns where necessary, so it is the cleaner and more maintainable choice.